    {
      "key": "gg.ammo.casings",
      "title": "Cases and Slugs",
      "tier": "LV",
      "desc": [
        "Every loose round in the LV press is two small GregTech parts plus gunpowder. The case is a foil: a thin brass sheet made in the Bending Machine. The slug is a round: a small metal ball made in a Lathe from a nugget, or by hand with a file. Lead rounds go into pistol bullets and shotgun pellets; steel rounds go into rifle bullets.",
        "Hold sixteen brass foils, sixteen lead rounds and sixteen steel rounds to finish. That is exactly one press run of each kind. Brass is a copper and zinc alloy; check NEI for how to make it.",
        "[note]Make plenty. A single 9mm batch eats sixteen of each part.[/note]"
      ],
      "pre": [
        "gg.ammo.intro"
